invariant: INV-14
file: src/jws.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh jws
reason: verify_es256 hands the P-256 check a signature of any length. The
  check reads 64 bytes, so a shorter signature makes it read past the
  bytes the token gave. bin/jws_test passes signatures from a room of
  1,024 bytes, so the read lands on the room's other bytes and the answer
  is still CH_EAUTH: no test sees the edit. The jws proof holds the P-256
  stub to a readable 64-byte signature and requires CH_EAUTH, with no
  verifier called, for every other length.

--- old
    if (sig_len != ES256_SIG_LEN) {
        return CH_EAUTH;
    }
--- new
    (void)sig_len;
